A||||4||Formula 18||Turbo Options? ||||1||
Z||000000||Formula 18||09-20-2000||08:00 PM||||Kinda long but the REAL question is below.<P>Here's the deal. I went to the Junkie today to get a turbo off a 86 T-Bird and while I was walking out there I saw a REALLY nice Pontiac Sunbird Turbo Coupe. I started to think if this would be a better match to a 2.8 (origanlly a 2.0 inline 4) b/c it would spool up at a low rpm due to a smaller turbine and with a wastegate it wouldn't run over like 8-9lbs. I didn't know if would be too much spin for the little guy. The also had a 2.2 DaytonaZ with a turbo (well two I think) and a 86 T-bird with the turbo.<P>So for like $60 should I take the turbo off a 2.0 Sunbird, 2.2 Daytona, or the 2.3 T-bird. <P>Side note, will the power seat from an 89 Sunbirn fit in the Fiero? The seem alittle taller but might work for $25.<P><P>------------------<BR>Brian<BR> -88 Formula||||reg||1
Z||000001||Xtreme Fiero's||09-20-2000||10:30 PM||||I would go with the 2.2 Daytona Z turbo, that car should have a Garrett T-25 or a T-3 either one can pump out 15psi (new wastegate) withs some porting you can run 20 PSI. that's plenty of juice. 20PSI would be way moer than enough for any street car. I'd keep it down around 8psi 10 if you have a goot knock sensor system||||reg||1
Z||000002||SCCA FIERO||09-20-2000||10:40 PM||||Might not be a good idea to use that little turbo from the Sunbird or the Daytona. It would build boost really fast, but after about 3000 RPM, the only thing coming from that turbo would be a huge restriction for the exhaust and a scorching hot intake charge. If you had an inter-cooler with anywhere close to 100% effenciency (only gonna find an inter-cooler like that on a marine application) you might last a few runs to the redline before the detonation toasted the motor.<P>The wastegate is the only thing that can save your engine. It is a very flawed, cumbersome invention. Say you set boost at 10psi. The wastegate will start to open around 5psi - only way to control boost though - and very ineffecient.<P>The turbo from the T-Bird would be the best choice. It's not water-cooled, but it has a better a/r for the 2.8.<P>------------------<BR>-Chris <BR>88 Fiero Coupe<BR><B>KEEP THE EXCITEMENT ALIVE!!</B>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Philphine||09-21-2000||01:49 AM||||2 sprint turbo turbos?||||reg||1
Z||000004||1FST2M6||09-21-2000||08:45 AM|||| <A HREF="http://www.turboneticsinc.com" TARGET=_blank>www.turboneticsinc.com</A>   or <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net</A>   the t-25 will not support more than 2.4 liters properly, the t-3 will but you'll be limited to boost pressure, to run the car all day with the fun tire shreading performance your probly looking for you'll need a T3-T4 hybrid or a TD04s. (stock unit from 86.5-93 supra) the new cars had water cooled housings for better durability and more consistant performance.  you need this...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> shhh jeff...  <P>Turbonetics external gate T-04<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newtoy2.jpg">  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newtoy.jpg"> <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 09-21-2000).]||||reg||1
